S('shipping-india-to-russia','Shipping from India to Russia: Sea Freight to Novorossiysk, St Petersburg, Vladivostok | YAM Logistics',
 'Shipping from India to Russia by sea and air: containers from Mundra and Nhava Sheva to Novorossiysk and St Petersburg, the Chennai to Vladivostok corridor, and export clearance in India by a licensed broker (R-7/92).',
 'Shipping from India to Russia','INDIA TO RUSSIA · SEA AND AIR','Shipping from India to Russia,','container and air cargo.',
 'YAM Logistics is a licensed customs broker (R-7/92) and freight forwarder in New Delhi. We move containers and part loads from Indian ports to Novorossiysk, St Petersburg and Vladivostok, and we handle the export clearance in India. A Russian-language version of this page is available.',
 [('The main sea routes',[('table',['Route','Indian ports','What to know'],[['Novorossiysk (Black Sea)','Mundra, Nhava Sheva','The shortest sea route to southern and central Russia. FESCO has put the direct sailing from Mundra at about 17 days, and about 10 days more with a transshipment.'],['St Petersburg (Baltic)','Nhava Sheva, Mundra','North-west Russia and Moscow. Published transit times for Nhava Sheva to St Petersburg run from about 50 to 65 days, usually with transshipment.'],['Vladivostok (Far East)','Chennai and east coast ports','The Eastern Maritime Corridor. The distance from Chennai to Vladivostok is about 5,647 nautical miles, against about 8,675 from Mumbai to St Petersburg via Suez.']],'Transit times depend on the carrier, transshipment and port conditions. We confirm the schedule before you ship.')]),
  ('What we do in India',['Collect cargo from your supplier and consolidate part loads at the warehouse.','File the shipping bill and clear the export as a licensed customs broker.','Book the container or the LCL space and follow the cut-off dates.','Send the bill of lading and the documents for the consignee, and track the vessel.']),
  ('Risk and planning',['Conditions in the Black Sea have changed from time to time, and some lines have added risk surcharges or changed the discharge port. We discuss the possible extra charges with you and put the terms in writing.','For cargo bound for Siberia or the Far East, the Vladivostok route can be shorter overall. For Moscow, the rail leg from Vladivostok is long, so we compare the full cost to the door.','Payment terms and any sanctions or licensing questions are for the parties to the sale to check before shipment. We handle logistics and customs clearance on the Indian side.']),
  ('Air cargo',['Urgent and high-value cargo, samples and medicines can move by air. Use the CBM calculator to work out the chargeable weight before you ask for a rate.'])],
 [('How long does it take to ship from India to Russia?','FESCO reports about 17 days from Mundra to Novorossiysk on the direct service, and about 10 days longer with a transshipment. Published times from Nhava Sheva to St Petersburg are about 50 to 65 days.'),
  ('Which Indian ports do you ship from?','Nhava Sheva (JNPT) and Mundra on the west coast, and Chennai and other east coast ports for the Vladivostok corridor.'),
  ('Do you handle the export clearance in India?','Yes. YAM Logistics is a licensed customs broker, licence R-7/92, and files the shipping bill for you.'),
  ('Is there a Russian version of this page?','Yes: https://www.yamlogistics.com/ru/dostavka-gruzov-iz-indii-v-rossiyu')],
 [('cbm-calculator','CBM calculator','Volume and chargeable weight.'),('ocean-freight','Ocean freight','Containers and LCL from India.'),('air-freight','Air freight','Urgent cargo by air.')])
